---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Build vs Buy" description="When should you build custom software vs use an existing tool? A practical guide for businesses.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm text-secondary hover:text-accent transition-colors mb-12 inline-block">← Back</a>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-text mb-6 leading-tight">Build vs Buy<span class="text-accent">.</span></h1>
    <p class="text-secondary text-lg mb-12">A practical guide for businesses deciding between custom software and existing tools.</p>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">The short answer</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">Most businesses don't need custom software. They need the right existing tool, configured properly, with maybe a small integration. But sometimes — and this is the key — off-the-shelf genuinely doesn't work. That's when you build.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">When to buy</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-secondary leading-relaxed list-none">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> The problem is common (CRM, accounting, HR basics)</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> Your workflow follows standard patterns</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> Speed matters more than customization</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> Budget is limited and timeline is tight</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> You don't have in-house technical capacity</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">When to build</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-secondary leading-relaxed list-none">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> Your workflow is unique to your business/region</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> Existing tools don't support Arabic/menA specifics</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> You need deep integration between systems</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> The software IS your business (SaaS, platform)</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent mt-1">→</span> You've tried existing tools and they genuinely don't fit</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">The honest truth</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">I've had clients come to me wanting a full custom build when they really needed a WordPress site with WooCommerce and a few plugins. And I've had clients who were drowning in spreadsheets because no existing tool handled their specific regional requirements.</p>
        <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-4">The right answer depends on your specific situation. I'll give you an honest assessment either way — even if it means I don't get a project.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block mt-6 bg-accent text-bg px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-medium hover:bg-accentHover transition-colors">Tell me about your problem →</a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
